# 🧠 What Did We Learn?

| ✅ Good Practice                                          | ❌ What Went Wrong                              |
| -------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| Remove debug endpoints before production                 | `/heapdump` was publicly accessible            |
| Protect diagnostic APIs with authentication              | Anyone could access the endpoint               |
| Restrict debugging functionality to trusted environments | A sensitive debugging feature was exposed      |
| Minimize sensitive data stored in memory                 | Sensitive information could appear in the dump |

