## 🔐 Key Takeaway

> **Debugging and diagnostic endpoints should never be exposed publicly without appropriate access controls.**

A heap dump can contain sensitive application data that was present in memory at the time of capture.

In a real-world application, exposing such an endpoint could lead to the disclosure of **API keys, credentials, session tokens, personal data, and other secrets**.

**Debug endpoints are valuable to developers — and potentially valuable to attackers.** 🚫🔓
